{"id":"VHH__tool__noise2d_cell","collection":"VHH","category":"tool","source_path":"VHH/tool/noise2d_cell.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::noise2d_cell"],"counts":{"nodes":74,"connections":136,"values":50,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Cellular Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a single frequency cellular noise similar to Worley noise. Full Credit to Duncan Brinsmead for the math.","documentation_search":"noise2d cell Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Cellular Noise - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a single frequency cellular noise similar to Worley noise. Full Credit to Duncan Brinsmead for the math. Input mask Scalar field mask on the outgoing field. warp vector field Domain warp on the outgoing field. field weight Overall weight of this field from 0-1. magnitude Magnitude of the field. frequency Frequency of the field. radius Controls the base height of the field. randomosity How random the cells are. time A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. seed The seed to use for randomization. adjust field An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values. translate Move the field. rotate Rotate the field. scale Scale the field. invert mask Inverts the scalar field mask. adjust mask A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask. warp amount The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp. sharpen When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp. At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field. step field When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\". step shape The shape of the steps. Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field. You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve. step mask A scalar field input to mask area of the step field. invert step mask When this is checked, the step mask is inverted. adjust step mask An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step mask. Output cellular noise field The field result ready to be used.","port_names":["adjust_field","adjust_mask","adjust_step_mask","cellular_noise_field","field_weight","frequency","invert_mask","invert_step_mask","magnitude","mask","radius","randomosity","rotate","scale","seed","sharpen","step_field","step_mask","step_shape","time","translate","warp_amount","warp_vector_field"],"node_types_search":["Core::Array::flatten_nested_array","Core::Conversion::degrees_to_radians","Core::Conversion::scalar_to_vector3","Core::Fields::advect_field","Core::Fields::fcurve_field","Core::Fields::field_is_empty","Core::Fields::fractal_turbulence_field","Core::Fields::gradient_field","Core::Fields::position_field","Core::Fields::scalar_field","Core::Fields::to_field","Core::Fields::transform_field","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::decrement","Core::Math::euler_to_quaternion","Core::Math::length","Core::Math::lerp","Core::Math::min","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::negate","Core::Math::subtract","Core::Type_Conversion::to_float","Unknown","VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field","adjust_the_field","get_offsets","iterate1","iterate2","maskWerks","step_funct","worley_noise2D"],"dependencies_search":["VHH::Core::Fields::change_range_field"],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::noise2d_cell","uri_imported":"stream:/bifrostGraphShape1","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/noise2d_cell.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Warp"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Field Weight"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Adjustment"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Mask"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Transform"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The steps"}]},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/noise2d_cell.md","documentation":"### ***noise2d_cell***\n<font size = 1>**Component Compound** - this compound is a component in the the *displacer* ecosystem.<br /><br /></font>\n<font size = 2>**Cellular Noise** - One of the pre-made noise fields.  This is a single frequency cellular noise similar to Worley noise.  Full Credit to Duncan Brinsmead for the math.</font><br />\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***mask***</span>\n<br />Scalar field mask on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***warp_vector_field***</span>\n<br />Domain warp on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***field_weight***</span>\n<br />Overall weight of this field from 0-1.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***magnitude***</span>\n<br />Magnitude of the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***frequency***</span>\n<br />Frequency of the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***radius***</span>\n<br />Controls the base height of the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***randomosity***</span>\n<br />How random the cells are.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***time***</span>\n<br />A scalar field with the time to sample the noise at. \n\n<span style=\"color:#62CFD9\">***seed***</span>\n<br />The seed to use for randomization.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_field***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing you to adjust the field across values.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***translate***</span>\n<br />Move the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***rotate***</span>\n<br />Rotate the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***scale***</span>\n<br />Scale the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_mask***</span>\n<br />Inverts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_mask***</span>\n<br />A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***warp_amount***</span>\n<br />The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***sharpen***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp.  At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***step_field***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\".\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_shape***</span>\n<br />The shape of the steps.  Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field.  You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_mask***</span>\n<br />A scalar field input to mask area of the step field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_step_mask***</span>\n<br />When this is checked, the step_mask is inverted.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_step_mask***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step_mask.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***cellular_noise_field***</span>\n<br />The field result ready to be used.","ports":[{"name":"magnitude","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"4f"},{"name":"frequency","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.25f"},{"name":"time","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"seed","direction":"input","type":"long","default":"9"},{"name":"translate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"scale","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"1f","y":"1f","z":"1f"}},{"name":"rotate","direction":"input","type":"Math::float3","default":{"x":"0f","y":"0f","z":"0f"}},{"name":"radius","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"1f"},{"name":"randomosity","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"1f"},{"name":"mask","direction":"input","type":"Core::Fields::ScalarField"},{"name":"adjust_mask","direction":"input","type":"Math::FCurve","default":{"version":"1","preExtrapolation":"0","postExtrapolation":"0","points":[{"point":{"locked":"1","interpolatio